Package: toxcalc
Title: US EPA Whole Effluent Toxicity Statistical Methods
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Rebecca", "Fisher", , "r.fisher@aims.gov.au", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An open-source implementation of the statistical methods
    specified in the US Environmental Protection Agency Whole Effluent
    Toxicity (WET) method manuals, recreating the capability of the
    discontinued ToxCalc software. Provides the EPA hypothesis-testing
    flowchart for deriving no-observed-effect and lowest-observed-effect
    concentrations, together with the minimum significant difference, and
    the point-estimation flowchart for median lethal concentrations and
    inhibition concentrations. Every analysis carries an audit trail
    recording which test was selected and which manual section justifies
    the choice.
License: GPL (>= 2)
URL: https://github.com/beckyfisher/toxcalc
